    {
      "quest_id": "lsh_the_prize_court",
      "title": "Everything Is Logged",
      "giver_npc_id": "stw_salvage_broker",
      "zone": "the_lashings",
      "level_min": 47,
      "level_max": 47,
      "description": "They keep books. Better books than the port does.",
      "objectives": [
        {
          "type": "kill_boss",
          "target": "Quartermaster Nadd Kell",
          "count": 1,
          "zone": "the_lashings"
        },
        {
          "type": "fetch",
          "target": "lsh_prize_tag",
          "count": 4
        }
      ],
      "reward_exp": 4420,
      "reward_gold": 17550,
      "accept_text": "The hull they call the prize court is where everything they take is logged and valued and divided, under articles, by a quartermaster.\n\nI want the books. Not to be righteous about it - I want to know who has been buying, because somebody in this port has, for twenty years, and it is not me and I would very much like to be able to prove that.",
      "turn_in_text": "[She reads for a long time.]\n\nFour names. Two of them are dead, one of them left with the Gadgetzan crowd, and one of them is still trading out of the Upper Yard.\n\nI am not going to tell you which. I am going to walk over there this afternoon and have a conversation, and whatever else happens, they are going to know that I know.",
