          "label": "the closing entry, to Harbourmaster Coil"
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "topics": [
            "lsh_two_columns"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "reward_exp": 3480,
      "reward_gold": 13800,
      "accept_text": "Every crate in, every crate out, which side of town it came from and which side it went to. People assume I keep the last two columns to be unpleasant.\n\nI keep them because in four years somebody is going to claim this town was always like this.\n\nWell. In four years somebody is also going to claim there was never a cove, or that it was nothing much, or that it fell apart on its own. Take Senna the closing entry and we will both have signed it.",
      "turn_in_text": "Signed, dated and filed.\n\nThat is the whole of my profession in one afternoon: something enormous happened, and the only part of it that will still exist in forty years is a line in a book that two people put their names to while everybody else was busy being relieved.",
